# CHANGELOG

Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/). Semver source: root [`package.json`](package.json). Release flow: [`README.md` — Version and CHANGELOG](../README.md#version-and-changelog).

## When to update

Any **user-visible or release-notable** change in a workspace package requires that package's `CHANGELOG.md` under `## [Unreleased]`. Do not finish the task without it.

| Changed paths | Update |
|---------------|--------|
| `packages/server/**` | `packages/server/CHANGELOG.md` |
| `packages/client/**` | `packages/client/CHANGELOG.md` |
| `packages/protocol/**` | `packages/protocol/CHANGELOG.md` |
| `packages/cli/**` | `packages/cli/CHANGELOG.md` |
| `apps/web/**` | `apps/web/CHANGELOG.md` |
| Monorepo-wide (root config, CI, multi-package features, spec docs) | Root `CHANGELOG.md` |

Multi-package work: update **each affected package** changelog **and** root `CHANGELOG.md` when the release spans packages or docs.

Skip changelog only for trivial chores with no behavioral or release impact (typo in comment, whitespace-only).

## How to write entries

- Add bullets under `## [Unreleased]` only — never edit past release sections.
- Use sections: `Added`, `Changed`, `Deprecated`, `Removed`, `Fixed`, `Security`.
- Imperative, user-facing wording; no commit hashes or file lists.
- Root entries may prefix scope: `**server:**`, `**web:**`, `**client:**`, `**docs:**`.
- Spacing: one blank line after each `## […]` heading, one blank line between release sections.

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

### Added

- Origin removal in operator app panel

### Fixed

- Hide developer routes when portal is disabled
```

## Release

Before bumping version, ensure `[Unreleased]` is filled in every touched package. Then:

```bash
pnpm version patch --no-git-tag-version
```

This promotes `[Unreleased]` → `[X.Y.Z]` and syncs all workspace `package.json` versions. Do not run `node scripts/promote-changelog-unreleased.mjs` alone.
